Title:
Rowan — Static security scanner for AI applications (SAST + model/dependency scanning)

Type:
GitHub Tool

Short Summary (4-8 sentences max):
- Rowan is a Python-based static analysis tool that scans source code, AI/ML model artifacts, dependency manifests, and agent/MCP configuration for security issues without executing the target project.  
- It aims to surface reviewable evidence for likely vulnerabilities such as injection, unsafe deserialization, SSRF, path traversal, XSS, leaked secrets, risky agent tools, and unsafe model loading.  
- The core SAST engine is Opengrep, using a sizable rule catalog (regex + taint/dataflow rules) with deeper cross-file analysis for Python and JS/TS.  
- It also supports software composition analysis (OSV CVE lookups, EPSS), plus SBOM (CycloneDX) and OpenVEX outputs, with an offline mode via `--no-sca`.  
- Rowan is useful for AppSec/Blue Teams and CI owners, and also for red teams/pentesters to quickly triage common bug classes and AI-specific footguns in repos.  
- Interesting because it explicitly targets AI app attack surface (models, prompt files, agent tools, MCP config) while keeping scans local by default.

Technical Focus:
- Opengrep-based SAST (pattern + taint/dataflow analysis)
- Cross-file dataflow for Python and JS/TS
- AI/ML artifact scanning (pickle/PyTorch/GGUF/SafeTensors/ONNX/etc. via Hayward)
- Dependency vulnerability lookups (OSV) and EPSS enrichment
- CI integration (exit codes, baselines, SARIF/JSON/HTML reporting)
- SBOM (CycloneDX) and OpenVEX generation

Use Cases:
- Add SAST checks to CI/CD with severity gates and SARIF output for code scanning
- Audit AI/ML repos for unsafe model loading and deserialization risks
- Detect leaked secrets and common web/app vuln patterns pre-release
- Track and suppress known findings using baselines; alert only on regressions
- Generate SBOM/OpenVEX artifacts for supply-chain reporting and remediation workflows

Keywords:
Rowan, rowan-sast, SAST, static analysis, Opengrep, Semgrep-compatible rules, taint analysis, dataflow, SSRF, unsafe deserialization, injection, XSS, secrets scanning, AI security, model scanning, pickle, PyTorch, SafeTensors, GGUF, ONNX, OSV, EPSS, CycloneDX, OpenVEX, SARIF, MCP, agent tools, CI baseline